Z||000000||carpetviper||09-29-2001||06:09 PM||||I need you guys to help me out on this one A.S.A.P. I have an '86 Fiero SE that seems to be burning oil I think. I've put about 7 quarts in it in about 3-4weeks. THIS IS NOT COOL! Anyway, if you pull out the PVC valve you can see black grit as the bottom and the oil on the dipstick is black instead of brown/translucent. Any ideas on the cause and how i can fix it without to much $?? Thanks for taking time to read. You can e-mail me at  <A HREF="mailto:Viper05315@aol.com">Viper05315@aol.com</A> .||||reg||4
Z||000001||samoht||09-29-2001||06:15 PM||||what size motor , and is it leaking out anywhere, white smoke in the exhaust, oil in the throttle body.. you need to do alot more research b4 anyone can help you||||reg||1
Z||000002||carpetviper||09-29-2001||06:39 PM||||I'm sorry, here. It's a V6 manual and no I cannot see any oil leaking out at any pitstops or when its just sitting somewhere. Also from a fried who followed me they said that when first accelerating from 1st gear they could see white smoke clouds, but none to higher shifting.<p>[This message has been edited by carpetviper (edited 09-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||samoht||09-29-2001||07:07 PM||||i would say that the easiest although unlikely would be a new PCV vavle. but consider how much oil your are losing prolly not..  it is prolly vavle seals. and while you have the heads off you can check the ridges in the cylinders walls cause you might have bad rings or to much clearance.. but considering all the gunk under your vavle cover I would try a vavle job.. prolly 120 dollars for the both of them and 50 dollars for a gasket kit.. you should get new head bolts if it is in your budget||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-30-2001||01:28 PM||||That kind of oil burning would likely produce large amounts of smoke pretty much all the time.... have you checked it for a leak?<P>A new PCV wouldn't hurt... would eliminate the posibility of a stcuk valve. <P>The crap in the motor is a bad sign. could be rebuild time...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
